==Finnish==

===Etymology===
Probably from Baltic *''sḗjlā'' (compare Lithuanian {{term|lang=lt|siela}}), along with other Finnish loanwords from Baltic languages of the same thematic group, see etymology sections of e.g.{{term|lang=fi|taivas||heaven}}, {{term|Jumala||God|lang=fi}}. Another line of explanation links the word with {{etyl|gem|fi}} language (compare Swedish {{term|lang=sv|själ}}, German {{term|lang=de|Seele}} and English {{term|lang=en|soul}}).

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# [[soul]]
# [[moving spirit]] {{gloss|one who provides significant impetus or guidance in a given venture, movement, enterprise etc.}}

